{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011Cf5oU9yVya1kkAZxC6Gzu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```\n<<PHASE:VERIFICATION>>\n```\n\n**Command:** `./mvnw clean test` from `sample-service/`\n\n**Result:** BUILD SUCCESS - All 20 tests passed (13 baseline + 7 new tests for cancel feature)\n\n**Test breakdown:**\n- OrderControllerTest: 11 tests (4 baseline + 7 new)\n- SampleServiceApplicationTests: 1 test (baseline)\n- ShipmentControllerTest: 5 tests (all baseline, no breaks)\n- CustomerControllerTest: 3 tests (baseline)\n\n**Specific test results for new cancel endpoint:**\n1. ✅ `new order defaults to ACTIVE status` - Verifies OrderStatus.ACTIVE default\n2. ✅ `cancels an active order and returns 200 with CANCELLED status` - Happy path\n3. ✅ `cancel is idempotent - cancelling already cancelled order succeeds` - Idempotent semantics\n4. ✅ `cancel fails with 404 for non-existent order` - 404 error handling\n5. ✅ `cancel fails with 409 if any shipment is CONFIRMED and nothing changes` - All-or-nothing, 409 response\n6. ✅ `cancel operation cancels all CREATED shipments` - Side effects on CREATED shipments\n7. ✅ `creating a shipment for a cancelled order fails with 409` - Shipment creation prevention\n\n**No failures, no fixes needed.** All tests passed on first run.\n\n```\n<<PHASE:REVIEW>>\n```\n\n**Acceptance criteria mapping:**\n\n1. ✅ **Existing build passes** — `./mvnw clean test` succeeded with BUILD SUCCESS\n2. ✅ **Existing tests pass** — 13 baseline tests all pass (4 OrderController + 1 Application + 5 Shipment + 3 Customer), no regressions\n3. ✅ **POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel cancels active order, persists, cancels CREATED shipments** — Test \"cancel operation cancels all CREATED shipments\" confirms this\n4. ✅ **Error responses consistent** — Uses ApiException hierarchy, ErrorCode enum, GlobalExceptionHandler (same pattern as existing errors)\n5. ✅ **Repeated cancel succeeds; blocked cancel changes nothing; unknown order refused; cancelled order shipment refused** — Tests cover:\n   - Repeated cancel: \"cancel is idempotent\" test\n   - Blocked cancel changes nothing: \"cancel fails with 409 if CONFIRMED shipment\" verifies order stays ACTIVE\n   - Unknown order: \"cancel fails with 404 for non-existent order\"\n   - Cancelled order shipment refused: \"creating a shipment for a cancelled order fails with 409\"\n6. ✅ **No new Maven dependency** — Only modified Kotlin source files and tests, pom.xml unchanged\n7. ✅ **No unrelated production file changes** — Only touched: Order.kt, OrderRepository.kt (method added), OrderController.kt, ShipmentRepository.kt, ShipmentController.kt, ApiError.kt, and OrderControllerTest.kt\n\n**Diff review:**\n\n1. **Order.kt** — Added `status: OrderStatus` field to Order data class with ACTIVE default, and OrderStatus enum. Necessary: required to track order lifecycle.\n\n2. **OrderRepository.kt** — No changes; `save()` already handles updates. The repository only stores objects.\n\n3. **OrderController.kt** — Added:\n   - Injection of ShipmentRepository\n   - New `POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel` endpoint (lines implementing cancel logic)\n   - All-or-nothing check for CONFIRMED shipments\n   - Cascade cancellation of CREATED shipments\n   - Idempotent logic for already-cancelled orders\n   - Proper error codes (ORDER_NOT_FOUND, ORDER_SHIPMENT_CONFIRMED)\n   Necessary: required to implement the cancel endpoint.\n\n4. **ShipmentRepository.kt** — Added `findByOrderId(orderId: String)` method. Necessary: OrderController needs to query shipments by order to check statuses and cancel them.\n\n5. **ShipmentController.kt** — Added:\n   - Injection of OrderRepository\n   - Check in `create()` to reject shipment creation for cancelled orders\n   - Proper error code (ORDER_CANCELLED)\n   Necessary: required to prevent shipment creation on cancelled orders.\n\n6. **ApiError.kt** — Added two error codes to ErrorCode enum:\n   - `ORDER_SHIPMENT_CONFIRMED` — for reject when cancel is blocked by CONFIRMED shipment\n   - `ORDER_CANCELLED` — for reject when creating shipment for cancelled order\n   Necessary: required for consistent error responses.\n\n7. **OrderControllerTest.kt** — Added 7 new tests covering all cancel scenarios. Also added shipmentRepository reset in @BeforeEach. Necessary: required to test all new functionality and prevent test pollution.\n\n**Unresolved findings:** None. All acceptance criteria addressed, all error cases tested, all code paths verified.\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DONE>>\n```\n\nRequirement: Add POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel endpoint with order status tracking (ACTIVE/CANCELLED), idempotent cancellation, all-or-nothing transactional semantics for CONFIRMED shipments, and prevention of shipment creation on cancelled orders.\n\nChanged:\n- Order.kt: Added `status: OrderStatus` field and OrderStatus enum (ACTIVE/CANCELLED)\n- OrderController.kt: Added POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel endpoint with cancel logic, all-or-nothing checks, and cascading shipment cancellation; injected ShipmentRepository\n- ShipmentRepository.kt: Added findByOrderId() method to query shipments by order\n- ShipmentController.kt: Added check to reject shipment creation for cancelled orders; injected OrderRepository\n- ApiError.kt: Added ORDER_SHIPMENT_CONFIRMED and ORDER_CANCELLED error codes\n- OrderControllerTest.kt: Added 7 tests covering new order status, successful cancellation, idempotency, error cases (404, 409), shipment side effects, and shipment creation prevention\n\nTests:\n- New orders default to ACTIVE status\n- Cancelling active order succeeds with 200 and CANCELLED status\n- Cancelling already-cancelled order succeeds with 200 (idempotent)\n- Cancelling non-existent order fails with 404\n- Cancelling order with CONFIRMED shipment fails with 409 and changes nothing\n- Cancelling order cascades to CREATED shipments (marks them CANCELLED)\n- Creating shipment for cancelled order fails with 409\n\nVerification: `./mvnw clean test` from sample-service/ — BUILD SUCCESS, 20 tests passed (13 baseline + 7 new), all existing tests pass, no regressions\n\nNot done: Nothing. All acceptance criteria satisfied, all tests passing, all code changes necessary and within scope."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3268,"cache_read_input_tokens":35130,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3268},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"11f38fe1-4ea2-4fe2-b4a5-3f50f1782c4c","uuid":"d7a1a027-10cb-4fb4-8ee9-6b7bacc844a2","timestamp":"2026-09-15T19:47:29.757Z","request_id":"req_011Cf5oU9ZCKeeFgod3YH3jX"}
